 61NI c  1978Me10: chemical separation. Measured E|g, I|g, by a                 
 61NI2c  Compton-suppressed Ge(Li) detector.                                    
 61NI c  1988Sa26: measured E|g, I|g by Ge(Li). Confirmed the presence of       
 61NI2c  215.6, 625.5, 947.3, 1014.4 and 701.1 |g rays. But presence of 190.8,  
 61NI3c  276.7, 443.5, 629.9, 820.9 and 1089 |g rays was not confirmed.         
 61NI c  Source produced by {+59}Co(|a,2n) (1988Sa26,1967Be12,1967Bo01),        
 61NI2c  {+60}Ni(d,n) (1967Sc02), and {+63}Cu(|g,2n) (1969Ri04).                
 61NI c  Decay scheme is from |g|g coin results of 1967Wa04 and energy sums.    
 61NI c  Other |g-ray studies using Ge(Li) detectors: 1982Gr10, 1977Wa03,       
 61NI2c  1971VoZX, 1969Ri04, 1967Be12, 1967Bo01, 1967Sc02, 1967Wa04             
 61NI c  Pre-1960 studies of x ray, |b and |g rays from {+61}Cu decay: 1958Bu07,
 61NI2c  1957Ku57, 1956Nu02, 1953En06, 1950Co05, 1950Ow03, 1950Bo34, 1949Bo16,  
 61NI3c  1949Hu21, 1948Co08, 1945Br02, 1938Al02                                 
 61NI c  From RADLIST code, deduced total decay energy is 2063 keV {I81}        
 61NI2c  as compared to 2238 keV {I1} from Q(|e) value. It suggests that the    
 61NI3c  decay scheme is reasonably complete                                    
